{
  "total": 171,
  "totalPage": 4,
  "page": 4,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cad7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2287,
      "bookHadithIndex": 151,
      "text": "It was narrated that Sa'ib said to the Prophet (ﷺ):\"You were my partner during the Ignorance period and you were the best of partners, you did not contend or dispute",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2287-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2287-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2287-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2287-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cad8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2288,
      "bookHadithIndex": 152,
      "text": "It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:\"Sa'd, 'Ammar and I entered into a partnership on the day of Badr, (agreeing to share) whatever was allotted to us. 'Ammar and I did not get anything, but Sa'd got two men (slaves)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2288-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2288-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2288-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2288-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cad9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2289,
      "bookHadithIndex": 153,
      "text": "lt was narrated from Salih bin Suhaib that his father said:\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'There are three things in which there is blessing: A sale with deferred payment; Muqaradhah (profit sharing); and mixing wheat with barley for one's house, but not for sale",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2289-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2289-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2289-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2289-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cada",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2290,
      "bookHadithIndex": 154,
      "text": "It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\"The best of your provision is what you earn, and your children are part of what you earn",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2290-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2290-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2290-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cadb",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2291,
      "bookHadithIndex": 155,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah that a man said:\"O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth and a son, and my father wants to take all my wealth.\" He said: \"You and your wealth belong to your father",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2291-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2291-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2291-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cadc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2292,
      "bookHadithIndex": 156,
      "text": "It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib, from his father, that his grandfather said:\"A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and said: 'My father is taking all my wealth.' He said: 'You and your wealth belong to your father.' And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Your children are among the best of your earnings, so eat from your wealth.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2292-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2292-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2292-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2292-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cadd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2293,
      "bookHadithIndex": 157,
      "text": "It was narrated that 'Aishah said:'Hind came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man and he does not give me enough for me and my child, except for what I take from his wealth without him realizing.' He said: Take what is sufficient for you and your child, on a reasonable basis",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2293-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2293-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2293-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2293-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cade",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2294,
      "bookHadithIndex": 158,
      "text": "It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\"When a woman spends\" and my father said: - \"When a woman feeds (the poor) from her husband's house, without spending too much, she will have her reward, and he will be rewarded likewise because he earned it , and she will be rewarded for what she spent. The same applies to the storekeeper, without anything being detracted from their rewards.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2294-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2294-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2294-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2294-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cadf",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2295,
      "bookHadithIndex": 159,
      "text": "Shurahbil bin Muslim Al-Khawlani said:I heard Abu Umamah Al-Bahili say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \" No woman should spend anything from her house without her husband's permission.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, not even food?\" He said: \"That is among the best of our wealth",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2295-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2295-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2295-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cae0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2296,
      "bookHadithIndex": 160,
      "text": "It was narrated from Muslim Al-Mula'i that he heard Anas bin Malik say:\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to accept the invitation of a slave",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2296-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2296-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2296-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2296-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cae1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2297,
      "bookHadithIndex": 161,
      "text": "It was narrated that 'Umair, the freed slave of Aabi Lahm, said:\"My master used to give me food and I would feed others from it, then he stopped me,\" or he said: \"He beat me. So I asked the Prophet,” -or- \"he asked him and I said: 'I will not stop.' He said: 'Both of you will be rewarded",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2297-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2297-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2297-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2297-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cae2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2298,
      "bookHadithIndex": 162,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Bishr Ja'far bin Abu Jyas said:“I heard 'Abbad bin Shurahbil, a man from Banu Ghubar, say: ‘We suffered a year of famine, and I came to Al-Madinah. I came to one of its gardens and took an ear of corn, I rubbed it, ate some and put the rest in my garment. The owner of the garden came and beat me and took my garment. I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and told him (what had happened). He said to the man: \"You did not feed him when he was hungry and you did not teach him when he was ignorant.\"' Then the Prophet (ﷺ) told him to give back his garment and ordered that a Wasq or half a Wasq of food be brought to him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2298-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2298-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2298-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2298-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cae3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2299,
      "bookHadithIndex": 163,
      "text": "It was narrated that Rafi' bin 'Amr Al-Ghifari said:\"When I was a boy, I used to throw stones at our date-palm trees\"[1] - or he said: \"the date-palm trees of the Ansar.\" I was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: 'O boy' - (one of the narrators) Ibn Kasib said: He said: 'O my son - why are you throwing stones at the date-palm trees?' I said: 'So I can eat.' He said: 'Do not throw stones at the date-palm trees. Eat from what falls to the ground from them.' Then he patted me on the head and said: 'O Allah give him enough to eat.'”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2299-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2299-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2299-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2299-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cae4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2300,
      "bookHadithIndex": 164,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Sa'eed that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\"When you come to a shepherd, call him three times. If he answers (all well and good), otherwise drink (milk from the flock) without taking advantage. And when you come to a garden call the owner of the garden three times. If he answers (all well and good), otherwise eat (from the produce of the garden) without taking advantage",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2300-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2300-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2300-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cae5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2301,
      "bookHadithIndex": 165,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\"When anyone of you passes by a garden let him eat therefrom, but he should not carry any away in his garment",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2301-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2301-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2301-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2301-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cae6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2302,
      "bookHadithIndex": 166,
      "text": "It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up and said:\"No one of you should milk from the livestock of another man without his permission. Would anyone of you like someone to break into his storeroom and take his food? The udders of their livestock store food for them, so none of you should milk the livestock of another man without his permission",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2302-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2302-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2302-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2302-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cae7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2303,
      "bookHadithIndex": 167,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah said:“While we were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey, we saw some camels with their udders tied, among some thorny trees. We rushed towards it, but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called us and we came back to him. He said: 'These camels belong to a family of Muslims, and this is their support (and blessing) after Allah. Would you be happy if you went back to your vessels and found that what was in them had been taken away? Do you think that is fair?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'This is like that.' We said: 'What do you think if we are in need of food and drink?' He said: 'Eat but do not carry any away: drink but do not carry any away",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2303-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2303-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2303-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cae8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 12,
      "hadithIndex": 2304,
      "bookHadithIndex": 168,
      "text": "It was narrated from Umm Hani' that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to her:\"Keep sheep, for in them is blessing",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2304-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-12-2304-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
